#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space for the latest version of "
"Qiskit bosons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bosonic-synthesis-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space {#synthesize-an-evolution-"
"gate-in-bosonic-space}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The time evolution $e^{-itH}$ of a Hamiltonian that is a sum of non-"
"commuting pieces cannot be implemented exactly gate by gate. A **product "
"formula** approximates it by a sequence of short evolutions under the "
"individual pieces, and the approximation error is called the Trotter "
"error.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can apply a product formula in two places, and they are not "
"interchangeable:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**In bosonic space**, before any truncation or encoding has been chosen. The"
" formula sees the *groups* of the operator (see [Group operator terms: use "
"the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)) and can interleave "
"them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**In qubit space**, inside Qiskit’s "
"[`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate),"
" after the operator has been mapped. The formula sees one Pauli operator per"
" group and can only subdivide the terms *within* it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Only the first can reduce the error between groups that do not commute, "
"which is usually the dominant one. This guide shows how to use it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Both steps are optional. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate that is never decomposed in bosonic space reaches the boson-to-qubit stage whole and is mapped and synthesized there. That incurs *no* error at the bosonic level, only whatever the qubit-level formula introduces.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up {#set-up}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A two-site Bose-Hubbard chain, the smallest example in which the groups do "
"not commute (see [Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of "
"encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) for the full model). It"
" is grouped into one Hermitian group for the bond and one diagonal group for"
" the on-site interaction:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To measure an error you need a reference. The exact evolution of the "
"Hamiltonian *as mapped at the same truncation* is the right one, because the"
" truncation is a separate approximation:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `error` deliberately simulates the lowered circuit *without* decomposing its [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) instances. [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) applies each as the exact exponential of its group, so the only thing left is the product of group exponentials that the bosonic synthesis chose.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The default {#the-default}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With no `synthesis` argument an "
"[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate decomposes with "
"[`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-"
"trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\"), the first-"
"order formula: one factor per group, each for the whole time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Without decomposing, the whole gate is handed to the qubit stage and there "
"is no bosonic Trotter error at all:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Decomposed, a genuine error appears, because the two groups do not "
"commute:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reduce the error {#reduce-the-error}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pass a different synthesis method to the gate. A higher **order** composes "
"the factors symmetrically so that the leading error terms cancel; more "
"**repetitions** divide the time into shorter steps.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each increase of the order by two composes five sweeps of the one below (the"
" $5^{(k-2)/2}$ growth of Suzuki’s recursion, applied to the $2n - 1$ factors"
" of order 2), which is the count in the last line, marked with a star. The "
"sweeps meet on the same factor, so the neighboring gates evolve under one "
"operator and are fused into a single gate with the summed time. That saves "
"one gate per seam and is exact. Pass `merge_adjacent=False` to keep the "
"textbook sequence. Either way, a higher order buys a smaller error:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Repetitions trade depth for accuracy at a different rate. The first-order "
"error falls linearly in the step size, the second-order one quadratically:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Which is the better trade depends on the operator. Note that an operator "
"with a single group is exact at any order, because a lone factor commutes "
"with itself, and the formula then collapses to one gate rather than re-"
"splitting it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Measure the cost {#measure-the-cost}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A smaller error costs more factors, and each factor costs entangling gates "
"once the qubit stage has synthesized it. How many depends on the encoding, "
"so count them through the preset pipeline, with the basis fixed and no "
"qubit-level optimization (`optimization_level=0`), to see the price of each "
"method:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The exact counts depend on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution gates, which"
" changes between releases, so the plot shows them rather than a table:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Grouped bar chart of the CX count for Lie-Trotter and Suzuki of order 2 "
"and 4, for the Gray and the unary encoding. The counts grow with the order, "
"and the unary bars are higher.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"bosons/bosonic_synthesis-10.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each group of bars is a method: Lie-Trotter, Suzuki of order 2, and Suzuki "
"of order 4. The order buys accuracy at a price that grows by the factor of "
"the recursion, and the unary encoding pays more than the Gray code for every"
" method because each of its factors maps to more entangling gates. Choose "
"the method for the accuracy that you need and the encoding for the hardware,"
" and keep the two choices apart: the bosonic circuit above never changes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Apply one method to a whole circuit {#apply-one-method-to-a-whole-circuit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To set `synthesis` on each gate, you must thread the choice through "
"everything that builds one. The "
"[`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-"
"passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") pass makes the choice once"
" for a pipeline instead. Its `config` names the method for each type of "
"gate, and it both selects the method and expands the gates:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A method can also be named, with the arguments for its `__init__`, instead "
"of being built: `B2BSynthesis({\"Evolution\": (\"SuzukiTrotter\", (), "
"{\"order\": 2})})`. The available names are those of the "
"[`B2BSynthesisPluginManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-b-2-b-synthesis-plugin-"
"manager#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.B2BSynthesisPluginManager "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.B2BSynthesisPluginManager\"), and "
"a method that is registered nowhere can be handed over as an instance, as "
"above.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With `apply=False` the pass only selects the method and leaves the expansion"
" to the point where it is wanted, for example to inspect the circuit first. "
"An atomic gate is never touched, not even tagged:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An unexpanded gate reaches the boson-to-qubit stage whole, where it is "
"mapped without its `synthesis` being consulted, so every method then "
"produces identical output.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An optional `filter` restricts it to the gates that benefit. Evolutions "
"whose groups all commute, such as a Hamiltonian made only of number "
"operators, are synthesized exactly at any order, so a higher order would "
"only add depth there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Restrict the pass to the gates that benefit {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-"
"gates-that-benefit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A purely diagonal operator makes the point concrete, because number "
"operators commute with each other. Its groups are exact at first order, and "
"the second order spends entangling gates for nothing:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both circuits are exact, so the second spends more entangling gates for no "
"gain. (The symmetric order-two formula applies the first group twice at half"
" the time each, and thus the cost depends on which group comes first.) The "
"`filter` takes a predicate over the "
"[`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode)"
" and leaves the rejected gates untouched, so one pass can raise the order on"
" the gates that benefit and keep the rest at first order. The predicate "
"below accepts a gate only when its operator moves bosons between modes, "
"which is when the groups fail to commute:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you run the pass again, nothing changes: the factors it emits are "
"*atomic*.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Atomic factors {#atomic-factors}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") marked `atomic` has no "
"definition, so [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-bosonic-"
"circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") leaves it in place "
"however often it is applied. A synthesis marks the factors it emits this "
"way, and so does [`BosonicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-q-"
"drift#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicQDrift "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicQDrift\") for the terms it "
"samples.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is more than tidiness. Splitting a Hermitian group further, term by "
"term, yields factors that are individually **not** Hermitian, and the "
"exponential of a non-Hermitian operator is not unitary:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Each factor must be Hermitian on its own. A Hermitian operator split into groups can produce non-Hermitian ones, such as a hopping term separated from its adjoint. Check with [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\"). An operator *without* groups is split term by term, and the qubit stage then rejects the factors with `Operator contains complex coefficients`. The symmetrization of an even order partially cancels the error of a non-Hermitian factor, so a wrongly grouped operator can look better at order 2 than at order 1 while still being wrong.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat a short step {#repeat-a-short-step}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a circuit-level alternative, build one short Trotter step and repeat it."
" [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat\") flattens the repetitions "
"into one circuit and leaves the boundaries adjacent, so passes can act "
"across them:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pass `insert_barriers=True` to keep the repetitions apart. A barrier is "
"mapped onto every qubit of the registers it touches, because an encoding "
"needs several qubits per mode and a mode has no per-qubit image of its "
"own:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `repeat` is unrelated to the `reps` of a synthesis method. A synthesis subdivides a *single* evolution into more, shorter factors. Repeating a circuit that holds one evolution merely multiplies its total time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Combine with a qubit-level formula {#combine-with-a-qubit-level-formula}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The two levels compose, and where both approximate, the accuracy of the "
"result is governed by the weaker of the two. Raising the bosonic order while"
" the qubit-side formula stays first-order buys little. See "
"`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` for the qubit-side formula. It keeps the Pauli "
"term order that the mapper chose, and so `group_wise()` can emit the terms "
"of each group adjacent to one another, and `simplify()` can pin a canonical "
"order instead.\n"
msgstr ""

